00:09:34.036 --> 00:09:38.926
Surrey Council is the case on both sides of whether the city owned Surrey City

00:09:38.926 --> 00:09:43.546
Development Corporation stays arms-length or moves inside City Hall. The company

00:09:43.546 --> 00:09:49.186
was created in 2007. City is sole shareholder to build on surplus land. Mayor

00:09:49.186 --> 00:09:53.686
Doug McCallum dissolved it in 2020. Former mayor Brenda Locke brought it back in

00:09:53.686 --> 00:09:59.826
late 2022. By 2023 it was on a former Safeway site across from City Hall. Locke's

00:09:59.826 --> 00:10:05.866
promised 10,000-seat arena, luxury hotel, conference space, homes and shops, plus center block

00:10:05.866 --> 00:10:10.626
beside Suri Central Station, including room for Simon Fraser University's medical school,

00:10:11.026 --> 00:10:15.866
the Cloverdale Fairgrounds, two towers near Gateway Station, and a dense mixed-use site

00:10:15.866 --> 00:10:16.226
in Newton.

00:10:16.906 --> 00:10:18.826
McCallum's reason is a campaign promise.

00:10:19.286 --> 00:10:23.706
He said Monday, this is one of those promises, to download the development corporation into

00:10:23.706 --> 00:10:26.086
City Operations, and this is the start of it.

00:10:26.086 --> 00:10:29.886
Council voted this week to end the terms of four independent directors.

00:10:30.366 --> 00:10:36.026
As of Wednesday, the board is three city employees, city manager Rob Costanzo, finance director

00:10:36.026 --> 00:10:39.806
Vipinsech-Dava, and chief capital program's officer Jeff Erison.

00:10:40.406 --> 00:10:44.926
Costanzo's report calls the integration fairly straightforward and says some projects still

00:10:44.926 --> 00:10:48.406
need special care because of partnerships and obligations already in place.

00:10:48.886 --> 00:10:50.246
Staff are identifying those.

00:10:50.826 --> 00:10:53.486
McCallum also promised in the campaign to cancel the arena.

00:10:53.486 --> 00:10:56.206
So whether that project goes ahead is still open.

00:10:56.766 --> 00:11:01.266
Council Harry Baines, the only counselor outside the mayor's majority, was the only

00:11:01.266 --> 00:11:05.766
vote against removing the directors on Monday and at the November 9th meeting where

00:11:05.766 --> 00:11:07.386
the first integration vote happened.

00:11:07.906 --> 00:11:13.286
His reason is that polling SCDC into regular city operations risks losing the flexibility,

00:11:13.726 --> 00:11:17.006
focus, and approach that make it a useful municipal development tool.

00:11:17.406 --> 00:11:21.086
He asked what happens to the company's staff and what any severance would be.

00:11:21.086 --> 00:11:25.986
Engineering manager Scott Newman said he would not discuss severance, citing privacy,

00:11:26.286 --> 00:11:29.266
and that the city is looking at ways to bring staff in where it can.

00:11:29.866 --> 00:11:32.906
Council Doug Elford declined to comment and left it to the mayor.

00:11:33.466 --> 00:11:38.126
What is on the calendar now is Wednesday's smaller board, with staff still sorting which project

00:11:38.126 --> 00:11:39.146
